{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And it shall depart.</b> That Ephraim not be jealous, because the Messiah is from the family of Judah. And if [it refers to] Hezekiah — because of the strengthening of his kingdom:" "<b>And the adversaries of Judah.</b> Their haters. And if concerning Hezekiah — concerning Aram. And behold, he will not besiege Ephraim to repay them their recompense for the days of Pekah:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Resolved the elliptical subject of חזקתו as מלכותו based on the parallel sense of royal consolidation; the phrase is compressed and the subject is implied rather than explicit.", 1 "Read לא יצור as 'will not besiege' (root צור); alternatively the reading could be understood as 'will not distress' (root צרר), but the preceding context of צוררי points to the former."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:29.053996422Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}